+
+## Usage reported for a turn
+
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits, and is handed the usage of the whole turn: the sum of every provider call the turn made, so a deployer recording cost or budget from the hook counts the tool rounds that came before the final answer rather than the last leg alone ([validated by: hands the hook the usage of every provider call in the turn, not only the last round](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- A round that reports no usage contributes nothing to that sum and hides none of it: the rounds that reported are still counted ([validated by: still counts the rounds that reported when another round reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
+- A turn where no round reported still reports no usage ([validated by: still reports no usage when no round of the turn reports one](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
+- A turn that ran no tools made one provider call, so its sum is that call's usage and the hook reports exactly what it reported before the turn-usage change ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
